// Title: Shadow AI - File Upload to Unsanctioned GenAI Web App
// Description: Detects users uploading files to public generative-AI web
//   apps (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude.ai, Perplexity, etc.) from managed
//   devices. This is a data exfiltration / DLP concern distinct from
//   traditional cloud storage exfil: sensitive data pasted or uploaded into
//   a third-party AI tool may be retained, used for model training, or
//   otherwise leave the org's control boundary with no corporate oversight.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1567 (Exfiltration Over Web Service)
// Data source: Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps, CloudAppEvents table
//   (M365 Defender / Sentinel unified advanced hunting).
// IMPORTANT PREREQUISITE - verified against Microsoft's documented
//   "Apps and services covered" list for CloudAppEvents: this table is
//   populated by APP-CONNECTED SaaS (Office 365, SharePoint, Teams,
//   Salesforce, GitHub, Dropbox, Atlassian, etc.) and by session-controlled
//   apps routed through Conditional Access App Control. Consumer GenAI apps
//   (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude.ai, Perplexity, etc.) have NO native API
//   connector - Defender for Cloud Apps only sees them at the Cloud
//   Discovery traffic level (an app was used, how much data moved), not at
//   this activity level (what file, by whom). This query will return ZERO
//   rows for those apps unless you've specifically published the app
//   through Conditional Access App Control (reverse-proxy session control)
//   - it is not a matter of enabling a policy or waiting for data, the
//   connector doesn't exist for these apps otherwise. Use this query as
//   written only for GenAI tools you've proxied that way; for pure
//   visibility into unproxied GenAI app usage, use Cloud Discovery
//   (Discovered apps dashboard / Cloud Discovery policies) instead - that
//   data isn't exposed through this table.
// False positives: Sanctioned/approved use of an AI tool not yet added to
//   your allowlist. Prefer driving this off your Defender for Cloud Apps
//   app catalog's "Generative AI" category and sanctioned/unsanctioned
//   status rather than the hardcoded app name list below, if your tenant
//   has that categorization enabled - the list here is a fallback for
//   environments without app governance configured.

let UnsanctionedAIApps = dynamic([
    "ChatGPT", "Google Gemini", "Bard", "Claude.ai", "Perplexity AI",
    "Character.AI", "DeepSeek", "Poe"
]);
CloudAppEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(1d)
| where Application has_any (UnsanctionedAIApps)
| where ActionType in ("FileUploaded", "FileUploadedToCloud", "Upload")
| project Timestamp, AccountId, Application, ActionType, ObjectName, IPAddress, DeviceType, OSPlatform, CountryCode
| order by Timestamp desc
